<title>MEXICO: FORECAST - Mexico 28-day Cetes seen at 21.22 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Mexico 28-day Cetes seen at 21.22 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Mexico's bellwether 28-day Cetes, or T-bills, are seen falling 139 basis points to 21.22 percent, and rates are also seen falling at longer terms, according to a Reuters' survey of nine Cetes dealers.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY   CHANGE</p>
<p>    28-DAY     22.61	    21.22		   -139 bps</p>
<p>    91-DAY     22.97	    22.19		   - 78 bps</p>
<p>    182-DAY    22.99	    22.51		   - 48 bps</p>
<p>    1-YEAR     24.29	    23.82		   - 47 bps</p>
<p>The results will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1830 (2330 GMT)</p>
<p>((- Mexico City newsroom 525 7289559))</p>
